.N.L.V., Kilo-G y las bases de Mannie Fresh, que tocaba con músicos en directo sobre la caja de ritmos. Ficharon a Juvenile y a los adolescentes Lil Wayne, B.G. y Turk y sacaron treinta y un discos en seis años vendidos en tiendas como Peaches. Wendy Day (Rap Coalition) les hizo un plan de negocio y los vendió como «el próximo No Limit»: en 1998 Universal firmó un 80-20 con los másteres de vuelta a los tres años. 400 Degreez de Juvenile («Ha», con remix de Jay-Z, y «Back That Azz Up») y «Bling Bling» de B.G. con los Hot Boys (la palabra llegó al Oxford English Dictionary): eran los ostentosos, frente a los soldados de No Limit. Hubo quejas por el dinero, pero Lil Wayne se volvió un gran letrista con sus mixtapes y su Young Money fichó a Drake y Nicki Minaj.","color":"#f472b6","family":"El Sur: Miami, Atlanta, Houston, Memphis, Nueva Orleans","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/ComeUp/#cash-money"}],"book_tracks":[],"mentions":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Target of Megan Thee Stallion's \"HISS\" (2024)","body":"Nicki Minaj was the target of Megan Thee Stallion's \"vicious beef record\" \"HISS,\" released in February 2024. The song, described as a \"slab of hate-a-rayed,\" became a surprise chart-topper and the first pure rap diss to reach number one on the Hot 100. \"her vicious beef record against friend turned rival Nicki Minaj, a slab of hate-a-rayed that she called HISS.\"","year":2024,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Here's The Beef Edition Part 2","url":null},{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Here's The Beef Edition Part 2","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4ef8154465cd600c50df"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Successor in Teen Pop","body":"Nicki Minaj is mentioned as a later artist who occupied the evolving niche of teen pop, succeeding earlier stars. \"se han ido viniendo en Nicki Minaj.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar 